any six from:
MP1. rub a polythene rod with a cloth and hang it from a thread (in a stirrup);
MP2. rub a second polythene rod and bring it near: they repel;
MP3. rub an acetate rod and bring it near the polythene: they attract;
MP4. two identical rods must carry the same charge, so like charges repel;
MP5. different materials gain different charges, so unlike charges attract;
MP6. polythene gains electrons and is negative;
MP7. acetate loses electrons and is positive;
MP8. use a dry environment for best results;
MP9. no charge forms on a metal rod held in the hand because it conducts;

